### COULD HAVE

---

**10. User-Initiated Withdrawal (exit vault position anytime)**
- **Purpose:** Basic custody expectation — user can pull capital out.
- **Target User:** DCA participant
- **Problem It Solves:** Trust — users expect to be able to exit.
- **User Value:** Reduces perceived custody risk.
- **Priority:** COULD HAVE
- **User Story:** As a DCA participant, I want to withdraw my remaining capital at any time, so I'm not locked in.
- **Acceptance Criteria:** User can call withdraw for their un-executed balance outside the DCA flow.
- **Success Metric:** N/A for demo scoring — not part of the core value proof.
- **Dependencies:** Feature 1.
- **Risks:** None significant, but easy to skip without hurting the pitch.
- **Out of Scope:** Partial withdrawal mid-execution, withdrawal fees/penalties.
- **Why not essential:** Not part of the problem statement's core loop or the judged decision journey — it's baseline hygiene, not differentiation. Build only if the core 7 MUST HAVEs are done early.

---

### REMOVE

---

**11. MEV Mitigation (private mempool / commit-reveal)**
- **Why reject:** High implementation cost (4h+), effectively unprovable in a live demo (you cannot stage a real sandwich attack convincingly in the time available), and the Context itself labels this a "design decision, not a PS mandate." Mention it as a narrated production consideration; do not build it.

**12. Real Keeper Network Integration (Chainlink Automation / Gelato)**
- **Why reject:** Already resolved in the prior strategy pass — adds an external dependency that can fail live during judging, for a capability (scheduled triggering) that the permissionless poke function already proves conceptually. Production-path narration only.

**13. Multi-Token / Multi-Pool Support**
- **Why reject:** Zero incremental judging value — the core claim (yield-while-waiting + market-aware execution) is fully proven on one pair. Adds surface area and testing burden for no differentiation gain.

**14. ML/Statistical Decision Engine**
- **Why reject (AI Value Test applied):** No training data exists; a black-box model is unauditable for a financial decision and cannot be verified by judges in real time; a deterministic rule achieves the same three-way decision with 100% reliability and full transparency. This was already REJECTED in the prior strategy pass — restated here for completeness since this task specifically asks about product features.

**15. Admin Dashboard / Analytics Beyond the Single Comparison**
- **Why reject:** Judges are evaluating one workflow, not an ops tool. Anything beyond Feature 8's single comparison metric is unused surface area competing for build hours.

**16. User Onboarding / KYC Flows**
- **Why reject:** Irrelevant to an on-chain, wallet-based protocol per Context §1 (explicitly forbids fiat/off-chain framing). Would actively contradict the domain framing.

