## PRODUCT → AI/ML HANDOFF

**No AI/ML capability is required for the MVP core.** This was tested explicitly (AI Value Test, Feature 3): the decision space is three discrete actions gated by two numeric signals, which a deterministic rule satisfies with full reliability and auditability — a hard requirement for an on-chain financial decision judges can verify.

**If the team wants to give the AI/ML specialist a legitimate task**, the only product requirement that would justify one is:

> *"If a genuinely predictive signal can be produced (e.g., short-horizon volatility forecasting) that measurably outperforms the deterministic TWAP-deviation rule on historical data, and that signal can be exposed as a simple, bounded score that plugs into the existing execute/partial/delay decision without replacing it — evaluate it as an optional enhancement input, not a replacement decision-maker."*

This is a strict boundary: AI/ML may inform a signal *feeding into* the deterministic engine; it does not own the execute/partial/delay decision. Not required for MUST HAVE scope.

